{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5hfXTXz3ZCmNfFkVro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `sqlmigrate` now only wraps its output in `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` when the migration is atomic **and** the database can roll back DDL (`connection.features.can_rollback_ddl`). Before, it only checked whether the migration was atomic. This matches what the migration executor already does.\n\nIt's a one-line change in `django/core/management/commands/sqlmigrate.py:60`, plus an updated comment above it.\n\nAll 88 tests in `migrations.test_commands` pass. The issue also suggests adding a test that mocks `can_rollback_ddl` to `False`, but I didn't add one because the rules said not to edit test files. No existing test covers the new case."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":19655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157},"output_tokens":230,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"500f4a82-58ab-48c5-ac7a-d44b3af5df0e","uuid":"1b998c89-00d6-4755-b719-d96dfb34d3f8","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:36:43.994Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5hfPXQWiq8YreqrvMi"}
